/**
 * @defgroup Foundation_Matrix Matrix
 * @ingroup Foundation_Math
 *
 * @brief Matrix types and algorithms.
 *
 * The Matrix module provides both fixed-size and dynamic matrix
 * implementations together with common matrix algorithms.
 * The entire family is enabled by `FOUNDATION_MATH_MATRIX`; applications
 * select the storage model when declaring each matrix.
 *
 * Matrix support is intended for:
 *
 * - Embedded systems.
 * - Digital signal processing.
 * - Robotics.
 * - Control systems.
 * - Numerical methods.
 * - Machine learning applications.
 *
 * @section FoundationMatrixOverview Overview
 *
 * Two matrix storage models are provided:
 *
 * - Fixed
 * - Dynamic
 *
 * Fixed stores its data directly inside the object and is intended
 * for applications where matrix dimensions are known at compile time.
 *
 * Dynamic allocates storage at runtime and is intended for
 * applications where matrix dimensions are not known until execution.
 *
 * @section FoundationMatrixTypes Matrix Types
 *
 * @subsection FoundationMatrixFixed Fixed Matrices
 *
 * Fixed-size matrices use compile-time dimensions:
 *
 * @code
 * Foundation::Math::Matrix::Fixed<float, 3, 3> matrix;
 * @endcode
 *
 * Advantages:
 *
 * - No heap allocation.
 * - Deterministic memory usage.
 * - Compile-time dimension checking.
 *
 * See:
 *
 * - @ref Foundation_Matrix_Fixed
 *
 * @subsection FoundationMatrixDynamic Dynamic Matrices
 *
 * Dynamic matrices determine their dimensions at runtime:
 *
 * @code
 * Foundation::Math::Matrix::Dynamic<float> matrix;
 * if (!matrix.Allocate(3, 3)) {
 *     // Invalid dimensions or insufficient memory.
 * }
 * @endcode
 *
 * Advantages:
 *
 * - Flexible dimensions.
 * - Runtime resizing.
 * - Owned heap storage or attached caller-owned storage.
 * - Non-throwing allocation-failure reporting.
 *
 * See:
 *
 * - @ref Foundation_Matrix_Dynamic
 *
 * @section FoundationMatrixOperationsSection Operations
 *
 * Matrix algorithms are provided separately from the matrix containers.
 *
 * Supported operations currently include:
 *
 * - Matrix multiplication.
 * - Fixed × Fixed multiplication.
 * - Dynamic × Dynamic multiplication.
 * - Fixed × Dynamic multiplication.
 * - Dynamic × Fixed multiplication.
 *
 * See:
 *
 * - @ref Foundation_MatrixOperations
 *
 * @section FoundationMatrixUsage Usage Examples
 *
 * Fixed-size multiplication:
 *
 * @code
 * Foundation::Math::Matrix::Fixed<float, 2, 2> A;
 * Foundation::Math::Matrix::Fixed<float, 2, 2> B;
 * Foundation::Math::Matrix::Fixed<float, 2, 2> C;
 *
 * if (!Foundation::Math::Matrix::Multiply(A, B, C)) {
 *     // Invalid dimensions, allocation failure, or overlapping storage.
 * }
 * @endcode
 *
 * Dynamic multiplication:
 *
 * @code
 * Foundation::Math::Matrix::Dynamic<float> A;
 * Foundation::Math::Matrix::Dynamic<float> B;
 * Foundation::Math::Matrix::Dynamic<float> C;
 *
 * Foundation::Math::Matrix::Multiply(A, B, C);
 * @endcode
 *
 * @section FoundationMatrixApplications Applications
 *
 * Common applications include:
 *
 * - Coordinate transformations.
 * - State-space control systems.
 * - Robotics kinematics.
 * - DSP filter structures.
 * - Linear algebra algorithms.
 * - Neural networks.
 *
 * @section FoundationMatrixRelated Related Modules
 *
 * - @ref Foundation_Matrix_Fixed
 * - @ref Foundation_Matrix_Dynamic
 * - @ref Foundation_MatrixOperations
 *
 * @namespace Foundation::Math::Matrix
 * @brief Fixed-size and runtime-sized matrix types and their algorithms.
 */
